course: dictionary
lesson: 7632
title: Putting things off
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Procrastination means putting off something you should do, especially something boring or hard, and doing it later or at the last minute. It is a noun. The verb is procrastinate, and someone who does it often is a procrastinator.
explain: «Putting things off is called procrastination, and everyone does it sometimes.» The clue is in the words put off: the work is still waiting, and you have chosen not to start it yet.
explain: «Putting work off to the last minute is called procrastination; a deadline is when the work must be handed in.» The deadline is the day the work must be finished, so leaving it until the last minute is the procrastination. Check by swapping in your meaning: "Putting work off is called putting work off" still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
fact: Procrastination is a noun: the thing itself. Procrastinate is the verb, meaning to put something off.
fact: A procrastinator is a person who often puts things off.
fact: People often procrastinate with tasks that are boring or hard, like homework or revision.
fact: Leaving homework until the night before is a common kind of procrastination.
fact: The saying «Procrastination is the thief of time» means that putting things off wastes time you could have used.
exercise: What does procrastination mean? | Doing a task early, so it is finished well before the deadline | Going for a long walk to clear your head | Forgetting your homework bag at home | *Putting off something you should do, and doing it later
exercise: «A deadline is when the work must be handed in.» What is a deadline? | *The day or time when work must be handed in | A kind of pencil | A type of homework book | A time for a party
exercise: Which word is the verb, meaning to put something off? | procrastinator | *procrastinate | procrastination | deadline
test: Ravi leaves his maths revision until the night before the test. Which word best describes him? | *A procrastinator | Brave | Organised | Early
test: «Procrastination is the thief of time.» What does this saying mean? | Thieves steal clocks from schools | Time always goes slowly in lessons | *Putting things off wastes time you could have used | Starting early always costs money
exam: Which tip from the lessons helps you stop procrastinating? | *Break the task into small steps and start with five minutes | Put the task off until tomorrow | Wait until you feel like doing it | Do the hardest task last of all
